  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nExplain an operation's height mismatch at generation instead of leaving only a rapid-move index to diagnose it.\r\n\r\n- For upright 2D/3D milling, compare authored Top against declared stock facets clipped to the operation's controlled region.\r\n- Credit earlier same-setup facing/pocketing through the existing lazy prior grid for analytic box/cylinder stock. Partial or unknown removal keeps the advisory. Sampled model-stock history is conservative because it can miss sub-cell raised features.\r\n- Store the advisory in existing toolpath notes and show it as a warning in the operation status banner. Existing move-level collision checks and post refusal remain unchanged; no NC moves, serialized warning variant, project-format version, or dependency is changed.\r\n- Retain current-main UI changes and update three real-rendered snapshots for the new visible warning count and named stock-top footer.\r\n- Keep the decision in `docs/decisions/104-top-stock-warning.md`. Existing entry/digest tests still prohibit entry/inert-word notes and require unchanged moves while allowing exactly the new independent Top warning.\r\n\r\n## Readings and pinning tests\r\n\r\nThe implementation follows the repository's Issue Law, Prime Directive, local quick-gate policy, existing same-setup prior-stock laws, and polygon intersection/linear-facet height geometry. No vendor implementation or proprietary material was used.\r\n\r\n- `generation_names_top_below_stock_and_keeps_the_rapid_gate`\r\n- `facing_to_top_removes_the_height_warning_but_a_shallow_face_does_not`\r\n- `top_at_the_stock_surface_has_no_height_warning`\r\n- `a_narrow_mesh_stock_feature_is_not_acquitted_by_an_unsampled_prior`\r\n- `stock_top_is_local_and_disjoint_stock_is_silent`\r\n- `a_sloped_stock_cap_is_read_at_the_region_not_its_far_vertex`\r\n- `prior_credit_is_regional_and_partial_removal_keeps_the_highest_cell`\r\n- `a_prior_with_no_finite_surface_is_unknown_not_clearance`\r\n- `the_top_stock_note_is_a_visible_warning_not_an_entry_fallback`\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nNative Windows/MSVC validation, integrated with main `a89ed46d679c22ef9736cfdc1ea015a37f7f3615`; final tested tree `fbdc1f6244358146ab1ef69184772cc783c6082f`:\r\n\r\n- `cargo test --locked -j6 -p camcraft-app --lib --test top_stock -- --test-threads=6`: 84 library tests and all 4 Top/stock integration tests passed. This source integration differs from the final tree only by the three subsequently reviewed snapshot PNGs.\r\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base a89ed46d679c22ef9736cfdc1ea015a37f7f3615`: exit 0, both selected steps passed. App: 848 passed, 0 failed, 9 ignored; UI: 378 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -j6 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0 on the final tested tree.\r\n- Independent static review and bounded current-main integration review passed. The three final goldens are exact copies of actual native renders; every changed row was visually inspected and their hashes bound to the tested tree.\r\n\r\nThe initial two named-warning regressions executed and failed before the fix. Earlier partial/failed attempts are not counted as final passing evidence. No hosted workflows were dispatched; this repository gates locally.\r\n\r\n## Limits\r\n\r\nThis is an advisory, not a new safety certificate or a new post blocker. Tilted, rotary, and turning frames do not receive a world-Z diagnostic; drilling keeps its existing named R-plane refusal. Model-stock history and boundary-cell padding may conservatively retain warnings. No machine execution, release, or hosted workflow dispatch is part of this contribution.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Explain below-stock operation Top heights during upright 2D/3D generation, with regional stock comparisons and credit for earlier cuts on analytic stock.\r\n\r\nFixes #104\r\n",
